# The laptop is Windows and everything that consumes these files is Linux: the ops workstation, the
# containers, and the GitHub runners. Without this, an editor or a script that writes CRLF turns every
# subsequent diff into a whole-file rewrite and every merge into a whole-file conflict - which happened on
# 2026-09-23 - and a Makefile with CRLF breaks GNU make outright, because the trailing carriage return
# becomes part of each recipe line.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
